// Distributed NATIVE-GATHER schedule, REVERSED-DECLARATION variant
// (TASK-0389). IDENTICAL in shape to `distributed_gather.sched.nuc` — 4
// compute workers row-band partition the outer `i` axis of the SpMV
// gather loop, host runs load/save — but it drives
// `prog.gather_revdecl.algo.nuc`, in which the gathered array `x` is
// produced BEFORE its gather-index array `col_idx`.
//
// Why this schedule exists
// ------------------------
// On a strict-FIFO host->worker channel (mp-tcp-bufsync / mp-tcp-poll,
// `wire::read_msg_expect`), the host Push order follows producer-
// statement position and the worker Wait order follows `data_in`
// traversal order. For the reversed-declaration program those diverge
// (host sends {val, x, col_idx}; the gather index-first traversal makes
// the worker wait {val, col_idx, x}) UNLESS the compiler reorders the
// worker's per-channel Waits to the host's per-channel Push order. That
// reorder is the TASK-0389 root fix; this schedule is the e2e fixture
// that exercises it. WITHOUT the fix this cell fails LOUD on
// mp-tcp-bufsync (a `read_msg_expect` seq/tag-mismatch panic); WITH it,
// the cell is byte-identical across all 7 tier-1 backends.
//
// Everything else matches distributed_gather.sched.nuc: partition shape
// (M=8 → 2-row bands), per-data transfer mapping (val/col_idx i-banded,
// x whole-array broadcast because its index dim is data-dependent /
// OPAQUE, y i-banded on gather), all-sync transfers, same reference.bin
// oracle. See distributed_gather.sched.nuc for the full rationale.

schedule for "../prog.gather_revdecl.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_val     on host;
    place load_col_idx on host;
    place load_x       on host;
    place save_y       on host;
    place gather_madd  on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Row-band partition the outer i axis. M=8, 4 workers ⇒ 2 rows
    // each, exact-divisible.
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // All sync transfers — same mapping as distributed_gather.sched.nuc.
    transfer val     : sync;
    transfer col_idx : sync;
    transfer x       : sync;
    transfer y       : sync;
}
